  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Since we need to multiply by $\\frac{2}{3}$, we split the whole into $3$ equal parts horizontally and ensure that $2$ of the parts remain shaded.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130839/assets/da5df2aa46309b3d1f3b8786ebf993c33342a8b4d6267338b512c0dea3227955.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\frac{8}{21}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{7}\\times \\frac{2}{3}=\\frac{8}{21}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
